    "interpretation": "The only deployable fallback is the relational selector, which selects the same action as the greedy policy in most cases regardless of whether that action is optimal. It therefore inherits greedy's errors instead of correcting them. A selective router can only add value when the declined arm is better on the declined cases; here it is not, which bounds the achievable benefit of ANY router on this configuration. Stage 3E did not face this limit because its fallback arm was an independent trained V2B expert."
